 #### Triplane NeRF with Diffusion Prior
-- [S1] The framework uses a triplane NeRF representation where scene codes are optimized jointly with a diffusion prior to handle sparse-view data and ensure end-to-end coherence.
-- [S1] Prediction Format: v-parameterization $\hat{v}_\phi(x(t), t)$ from [43], such that $\hat{x} = \alpha(t)x(t) - \sigma(t)\hat{v}$.
-- [S1] Weighting Function $w(t)$: Uses SNR-based weighting $w(t) = (\alpha(t)/\sigma(t))^2\omega$ from Eq. (5), instead of LSGM mechanisms.
-- [S1] Scene code $\xi_i$: Shape $\mathbb{R}^{3 \times 6 \times 128 \times 128}$, representing a triplane NeRF representation.
-- [S1] Denoising Network Input/Output: Noisy and denoised triplane features, with channels of all three planes stacked together.
-- [S1] Denoising Network Architecture: U-Net with 122M parameters.
+- **Definition:** A framework using a triplane NeRF representation where scene codes are optimized jointly with a diffusion prior to handle sparse-view data and ensure end-to-end coherence [S1].
+- **Parameters:** Uses v-parameterization $\hat{v}_\phi(x(t), t)$ such that $\hat{x} = \alpha(t)x(t) - \sigma(t)\hat{v}$. Uses SNR-based weighting $w(t) = (\alpha(t)/\sigma(t))^2\omega$ in the diffusion loss [S1].
+- **Layout:** Scene code $x_i \in \mathbb{R}^{3 \times 6 \times 128 \times 128}$. Denoising network is a U-Net with 122M parameters, taking noisy/denoised triplane features with stacked channels [S1].
 
 #### EG3D Triplane Representation
-- [S2] Render feature image $I_f \in \mathbb{R}^{32 \times 128 \times 128}$ and raw RGB image $I_{128} \in \mathbb{R}^{3 \times 128 \times 128}$ by accumulating points along rays and performing volume rendering.
-- [S2] Extract dense depth map $I_D \in \mathbb{R}^{128 \times 128}$ from the volume rendering.
-- [S2] Feed $I_f$ and $I_{128}$ into a 2D super-resolution network to yield final output $I_{512} \in \mathbb{R}^{3 \times 512 \times 512}$.
-- [S2] SuperRes($I_f, I_{128}$) = $I_{512}$.
-- [S2] Image resolution: 512x512 for input images and final output.
-- [S2] Triplane representation $T$ is a tensor in $\mathbb{R}^{256 \times 256 \times 96}$, corresponding to 3 axis-aligned planes (xy, xz, yz), each with 32 channels and resolution 256x256.
-- [S2] Rendering speed: 42 fps on RTX 3090.
+- **Steps:** Renders feature image $I_f \in \mathbb{R}^{32 \times 128 \times 128}$ and raw RGB image $I_{128} \in \mathbb{R}^{3 \times 128 \times 128}$ via volume rendering. Extracts dense depth map $I_D \in \mathbb{R}^{128 \times 128}$. Feeds $I_f$ and $I_{128}$ into a 2D super-resolution network to yield $I_{512} \in \mathbb{R}^{3 \times 512 \times 512}$ [S2].
+- **Formula:** $\text{SuperRes}(I_f, I_{128}) = I_{512}$ [S2].
+- **Parameters:** Input and output resolution 512x512 [S2].
+- **Layout:** Triplane representation $T \in \mathbb{R}^{256 \times 256 \times 96}$, corresponding to 3 axis-aligned planes (xy, xz, yz), each with 32 channels and resolution 256x256 [S2].
